        "answer": {
          "short": "The 460 g jar: approximately \\$20.43/kg, compared with \\$22.14/kg for the 280 g jar and \\$20.86/kg for the 350 g container.",
          "worked": "Convert to kilograms: $280\\text{ g}=0.280\\text{ kg}$, $460\\text{ g}=0.460\\text{ kg}$ and $350\\text{ g}=0.350\\text{ kg}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{280 g jar unit price}&=\\frac{6.20}{0.280}=\\frac{155}{7}\\text{ dollars/kg}\\\\\\text{280 g jar unit price}&\\approx\\$22.14/\\text{kg}\\\\\\text{460 g jar unit price}&=\\frac{9.40}{0.460}=\\frac{470}{23}\\text{ dollars/kg}\\\\\\text{460 g jar unit price}&\\approx\\$20.43/\\text{kg}\\\\\\text{350 g container unit price}&=\\frac{7.30}{0.350}=\\frac{146}{7}\\text{ dollars/kg}\\\\\\text{350 g container unit price}&\\approx\\$20.86/\\text{kg}\\end{align*}$$\nThe 460 g jar is the best buy because its price per kilogram is lowest.",
